1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,550
One date on the can says “safe”, another says “tasty”.

2
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:06,110
They are not the same.

3
00:00:06,610 --> 00:00:07,590
Imagine:

4
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:10,550
you walk into a store and pick up a can of food.

5
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:13,110
You see the date and relax.

6
00:00:13,610 --> 00:00:16,020
But what does this date actually mean?

7
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:20,100
First, learn the difference between the labels.

8
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:25,580
Production date shows when the product was made.

9
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:29,640
Expiry date: the product is safe until this date.

10
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:32,740
“Best before” is a quality date.

11
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:36,590
Do not eat an expired product.

12
00:00:37,090 --> 00:00:40,520
Second, don't blindly trust dry goods.

13
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:49,320
Rice, pasta and flour last long if stored properly, but moisture and insects can spoil them early.

14
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:51,860
Third, look at the can.

15
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:57,290
If it is swollen, leaking, badly rusted or its seams are damaged, do not eat it.

16
00:00:57,790 --> 00:00:59,040
The most dangerous thing is botulism:

17
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:02,070
a disease that can cause severe poisoning.

18
00:01:02,070 --> 00:01:04,750
A dangerous can sometimes looks fine from outside.

19
00:01:04,750 --> 00:01:07,970
So never taste a suspicious can to check it.

20
00:01:08,470 --> 00:01:11,690
Fourth, dairy products.

21
00:01:11,690 --> 00:01:16,520
If the smell or look has changed, do not drink it.

22
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:22,640
Even if the smell is normal, it doesn't fully guarantee safety.

23
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:25,300
In the store, do three things.

24
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:26,600
Check the date.

25
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:29,400
Make sure the package is intact.

26
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:31,560
Follow the storage conditions.

27
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:35,220
Don't buy a suspicious product just because it's cheap.

28
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:39,750
You can save money, but it's not worth risking your health.

29
00:01:40,250 --> 00:01:43,680
Send a photo of the product label to our bot:

30
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:44,590
@sahiychishopbot.

31
00:01:44,590 --> 00:01:49,650
It explains what the label means and teaches you how to check, step by step.

32
00:01:50,150 --> 00:01:52,980
Send this video to your loved ones too:

33
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:55,810
it may save someone from a serious mistake.

